---
<Service
  slug="eri-scores"
  title="ERI Scores in Spokane | Bell Energy Solutions"
  description="Energy Rating Index (ERI) scores for builders and designers in Spokane County and Kootenai County, from a BSI Level 2 Verifier."
  heading="ERI Scores"
  lead="Energy Rating Index (ERI) scores show the results of design and third-party testing, produced by a Building Science Institute (BSI) Level 2 Verifier."
  photo="ERI field verification"
>
  <h2>Proof of the results</h2>
  <p>After consulting, design, and third-party testing, an ERI score shows the results and proves the home is comfortable and quality-built.</p>

  <h2>What an ERI score measures</h2>
  <p>The Energy Rating Index (<span class="term">ERI</span>) is a numerical score of a home's energy performance compared with a reference home, as defined by ANSI/RESNET/ICC Standard 301. A lower score means a more efficient home.</p>
  <p>ERI scores can be used in ENERGY STAR and DOE Zero Energy Ready Home certification.</p>

  <h2>Who it's for</h2>
  <p>Builders, architects, engineering firms, and home designers who need an ERI score for a project.</p>

  <dl class="spec" slot="aside" style="margin-top:20px">
    <div><dt>Verifier</dt><dd>Building Science Institute (BSI) Level 2 Verifier</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Credentials</dt><dd>ENERGY STAR Verifier and ENERGY STAR Partner; DOE Zero Energy Ready Home certified</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Area</dt><dd>{serviceArea.line}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Pricing</dt><dd>{business.quoteLine}</dd></div>
  </dl>
</Service>
